      ],
      "title": "Factorising Quadratics (a ≠ 1)",
      "content": "<p>When the coefficient of \\(x^2\\) is not 1, use the <strong>ac method</strong> (also called split-the-middle or grouping).</p><p>For \\(ax^2 + bx + c\\):<br>1. Multiply \\(a \\times c\\)<br>2. Find two numbers that multiply to \\(ac\\) and add to \\(b\\)<br>3. Split the middle term using these two numbers<br>4. Group into two pairs and factorise each pair<br>5. Write the final factorisation</p><p>Example: \\(2x^2 + 7x + 3\\). \\(ac = 6\\). Numbers: 1 and 6 (multiply to 6, add to 7). Split: \\(2x^2 + x + 6x + 3\\). Group: \\(x(2x+1) + 3(2x+1)\\). Answer: \\((2x+1)(x+3)\\).</p>",
      "example": "<p><strong>Factorise</strong> \\(3x^2 + 10x + 8\\)</p><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> \\(ac = 3 \\times 8 = 24\\)</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Numbers: 4 and 6 (\\(4 \\times 6 = 24\\), \\(4 + 6 = 10\\))</p><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> \\(3x^2 + 4x + 6x + 8\\)</p><p><strong>Step 4:</strong> \\(x(3x + 4) + 2(3x + 4)\\)</p><p><strong>Answer:</strong> \\((3x + 4)(x + 2)\\)</p>"
    },
